101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The proposed solution aims to detect student isolation in classrooms using computer vision and machine learning technologies. By leveraging the YOLO object detection model, the system will monitor physical distances between students to identify those who are isolated from their peers in real-time. Additionally, it will utilize facial recognition to track individual students, logging their isolation patterns over time. The system will generate reports that summarize these isolation patterns and flag students who are at risk of prolonged social withdrawal, allowing educators to intervene early. A user-friendly interface built with custom Tkinter will enable educators to view real-time data and access reports to support student well-being.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
