endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 353 0 R
/E (Research into classroom monitoring has long focused on tracking student engagement, participation, and behavior through manual observation. However, these methods are time-consuming and prone to human error. Studies like those by [Smith, 2017] and [Johnson, 2018] explored manual and digital techniques for identifying behavioral patterns in students. While these approaches were useful, they were limited in scalability and real-time accuracy.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 354 0 R
/E (The need for automated systems to track student behavior was highlighted in [Doe & Harrison, 2019], which emphasized the importance of real-time detection to prevent long-term psychological harm in students experiencing isolation. The study suggested that machine learning models could greatly enhance accuracy in detecting patterns of disengagement.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
