175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2. Use of Computer Vision for Human Interaction Detection Computer vision technologies, especially those involving object detection models like YOLO \(You Only Look Once\), have seen widespread applications in human activity recognition, including crowd analysis and identifying isolated individuals in social settings. Studies by [Kim et al., 2020] demonstrated how YOLO models could be used to detect crowd densities in public spaces. This technology has been applied in fields like security and retail but has the potential to address student isolation as well. Recent advancements in computer vision allow for real-time monitoring of physical distances between individuals, which is central to identifying isolation in classrooms. [Patel & Singh, 2021] applied YOLO to detect social distancing during the COVID-19 pandemic, which could be adapted to measure classroom seating arrangements and identify isolated students.)
/E (2. Use of Computer Vision for Human Interaction Detection Computer vision technologies, especially those involving object detection models like YOLO \(You Only Look Once\), have seen widespread applications in human activity recognition, including crowd analysis and identifying isolated individuals in social settings. Studies by [Kim et al., 2020] demonstrated how YOLO models could be used to detect crowd densities in public spaces. This technology has been applied in fields like security and retail but has the potential to address student isolation as well. Recent advancements in computer vision allow for real-time monitoring of physical distances between individuals, which is central to identifying isolation in classrooms. [Patel & Singh, 2021] applied YOLO to detect social distancing during the COVID-19 pandemic, which could be adapted to measure classroom seating arrangements and identify isolated students.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
